) is running."]}, "overview": "Mississippi's Senate race pairs incumbent Republican Cindy Hyde-Smith against Democrat Scott Colom, with independent Ty Pinkins also on the ballot. The state's partisan lean favors Republicans by about eleven points, and Hyde-Smith holds the advantages of incumbency and a cash edge, though Colom has raised a surprisingly competitive sum and drawn national Democratic support, including a campaign visit from Cory Booker.\n\nEvery major race rater scores the contest as at least Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-ten chance. The only recent independent poll, from August, showed Hyde-Smith ahead by six, but polling here is sparse and dated, keeping uncertainty elevated. The forecast expects a Republican win in the low double digits, with Colom's late momentum the main variable to watch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0354, "margin": -10.93}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0452, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0338, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0557, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0878, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0513, "margin": -11.0}]}